A||||7||bsuddath||Fun places to drive in northern California||||1||
Z||000000||bsuddath||08-17-2001||02:52 AM||||I am new to Northern California and want a chance to push the limits of my Fiero, mostly around corners.<P>Are there any members here who can recommend stretches of road that would be suitable.  Ideally, they would not be well travelled to minimize any risks to other vehicles||||reg||1
Z||000001||artherd||08-17-2001||03:07 AM||||Hrmmmm, drive west untill you hit water.<P>Turn North.  Or South.  enjoy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Seriously, there's the classic Highway 1 of ccourse (a MUST if you've never driven it!!!)<P>And north of Marin County there are literally thousands of miles of windy twisty 2-lane roads through the country, through redwoods, along the coast, cutting through mountians, etc.<P>It would be easier to list where not to drive, which is basically in cities and 4-lane highways.   Besides that, it's all Fiero country here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000002||coolcat||08-17-2001||03:24 AM||||Hey there,welcome to Sac  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">If you got a couple of gallons of gas to spare I'd have to say HW 50 at about 1am just start heading for Tahoe. Or another and safer place would be Sears Point Raceway.hope this helps ya.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headbang.gif"> Gettin good players is easy,gettin them to play together is the hard part||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||08-17-2001||09:57 AM||||Jeez, what part of Northern California doesn't have fun places to drive?  Highway 49 through the Mother Lode area is my fave, from Copperopolis to Jackson. Make sure you stop off in Mokluomnee Hill and go to the little bar at the bottom of the hill.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||08-17-2001||10:20 AM||||Was in Oregon, a few weeks ago. If the roads in northern Cal are anything like Oregon, they are pretty much *all* worthy of a Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||08-17-2001||10:43 AM||||Another nice drive near by that can include a  little hiking/walking would be roads around Lake Berryessa.  I've scared the hell out of myself a few times ripping around there in a car and especially on a motorcycle.  Believe me, you don't want to lose it and go OFF the road.  Here's a picture of the Monticello Dam that can be part of the ride.  Check that "Glory Hole".  It's kinda of cool to walk inside of that big ol' tube.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/montecellodam.jpg">   If you have enough traction, you can see blue sky from inside it. Follow the little red arrow. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/follow.jpg">  Go through Davis then Winters and past Salono Lake(puddle) and your there.<P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||stsmithgt||08-17-2001||10:58 AM||||Come to think of it.  My car is up there on Fulton Ave. at Braley and Graham's.  If I get it out of the shop THIS weekend on Saterday, I'll take a rip up there myself to test out the work done on my car because I'll be hanging out in Davis or around 55th street at a buddy's place in Sacramento.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||08-17-2001||12:54 PM||||Right, 49 over the whole length is a great drive.||||reg||1
